--
--   Description
----------------------
-- This test checks the handling of very short frames by the receive path.
-- NOTE : PCS mode will not run at 32-bit DMA mode because of 
--        bandwidth limitations. Test will be run at 64 bits instead.
--
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- * Checks the start of data detection of gem_rx
-- * Checks that preamble and SFD only frames are not falsely recognised
-- * Checks that 1 byte frame can be recognised and reported
-- * Checks that code errors are recognised in preamble and SFD.
-- * Checks that varying length preamble is received OK (including odd nibbles).
--
--  
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- 1. Setup DMA wait states for the test.
-- 2. Initialise the GEM for 1Gbits/s, TBI, 64-bit DMA mode.
-- 3. Enable all interrupts, and then enable receive.
-- 4. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
-- 5. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble and SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
-- 6. Receive a frame consisting of only SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
-- 7. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and one byte of data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize & bad CRC frame status.
--    (Note that bad CRC and too short will not get reported in a statistic)
-- 9. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and four bytes of data (good
--    CRC). Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize frame status.
--10. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--11. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
--12. Set the no FCS bit in the network configuration register.
--13. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and four bytes of data (good
--    CRC). Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize frame status.
--14. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and five bytes of data (good
--    CRC). Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize frame status.
--15. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--16. Check statistics for the above operations.
--17. Reset the no FCS bit in the network configuration register.
--
--18. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble that has a code error.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--19. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble and SFD that has a code error
--    during the SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--20. Receive a frame consisting of only SFD, with a code error.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--21. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and one byte of data, with
--    a code error during the byte of data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status. This is because code
--    errors are only reported in gigabit mode if length checks are satisfied.
--22. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and one byte of data, with
--    a code error during the SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status. This is because code
--    errors are only reported in gigabit mode if length checks are satisfied.
--23. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and one byte of data, with
--    a code error during the preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status. This is because code
--    errors are only reported in gigabit mode if length checks are satisfied.
--24. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--25. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
--26. Set the copy all frames bit in the network configuration register.
--27. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--28. Receive a frame consisting of only preamble and SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--29. Receive a frame consisting of only SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with no status.
--30. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and one byte of data.
--    Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize & bad CRC frame status.
--    (Note that bad CRC and too short will not get reported in a statistic)
--32. Receive a frame consisting of preamble, SFD and four bytes of data (good
--    CRC). Ensure that the frame is dropped with an undersize frame status.
--33. Receive a 64 byte frame with good CRC.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--34. Check statistics for the above operations.
--
--35. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has 0 preamble bytes, and
--    valid SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--36. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has 1 preamble byte, and
--    valid SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--37. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has 2 preamble bytes, and
--    valid SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--38. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has 3 preamble bytes, and
--    valid SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--39. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has 7 preamble bytes, but
--    has corrupted SFD (make sure data does not have "d5" in it).
--    Ensure that the frame is not recognised.
--40. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC that has corrupted preamble, but
--    has valid SFD.
--    Ensure that the frame is not recognised.
--41. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC, preamble, and SFD. This time
--    the data consists of all 55's (preamble).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--42. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC, preamble, and SFD. This time
--    the data consists of all 5d's (SFD).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--43. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC, preamble, and SFD. This time
--    the data consists of all 5d's (reversed SFD).
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--45. Receive a 64 bytes frame with valid CRC, and SFD. This time
--    the data consists of all 5d's (reversed SFD) and no preamble.
--    Ensure that the frame is successfully received, with good status.
--46. Check statistics for the above operations.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

